          "url": "https://spacemaneffects.com/products/polaris/",
          "host": "spacemaneffects.com",
          "title": "Polaris: Resonant Overdrive - Cadet Series - Spaceman Effects",
          "h1": "Polaris Cadet: Resonant Overdrive",
          "description": "Polaris is a smooth dynamic overdrive, with incredibly flexible tone-shaping capabilities. Featuring a 2-pole resonant filter, fully controllable via expression pedal for filter sweeps and out-of-this-world overdrive tones.",
          "snippet": "Polaris: Resonant Overdrive - Cadet Series - Spaceman Effects",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Polaris: Resonant Overdrive - Cadet Series - Spaceman Effects - | / Save up to % Save % Save up to Save Sale Sold out In stock Menu Pedals PDX Custom Series Cadet Series SpaceMod Series NOS Equipment Merch About Dealers Login 0 Login 0 Your Cart is Empty Continue Shopping $0.00 USD Subtotal Taxes and shipping calculated at checkout Checkout Pedals PDX Custom Series Cadet Series SpaceMod Series NOS Equipment Merch About Dealers \" /> \" /> \" > \" > Polaris Cadet: Resonant Overdrive Title Default Title Buy Now $199.00 Polaris is a smooth dynamic overdrive, with incredibly flexible tone-shaping capabilities. Featuring a 2-pole resonant filter, fully controllable via expression pedal for filter sweeps and out-of-this-world overdrive tones. Videos Meridian Polaris is a dynamic medium-gain overdrive, with incredibly flexible tone-shaping capabilities. Its unique feature set includes an optional 2-pole resonant filter, controllable via expression pedal for filter sweeps and out-of-this-world overdrive tones. Designed to help you explore the outer-limits of harmonic overdrive, Polaris&rsquo;s Drive control goes from just a touch of harmonics to full-tilt, live-wire overdrive on the brink of distortion, while staying reactive to your instrument and dynamics for an experience that&rsquo;s addicting. EXTREME TONE SHAPING The shining beacon of Polaris is contained within the unique tone shaping center at the heart of its control panel. Four out of the six controls are purely for tonal adjustments. The Filter control is the star of the show, an extremely effective control with three filter options, selectable via the Depth toggle switch above it. First position is a standard, single-pole low pass filter to adjust the high-end content. In the middle, you&rsquo;ll find a deeper 2-pole filter for serious sculpting. Last and certainly far from least, is the 2-pole resonant filter for the most extreme shaping. The Bass toggle switch offers three options for keeping your low frequencies under control. Whether you need a tasteful bass cut or boost, or you simply want them untouched, Polaris has you covered. The Initial control blends in your raw, pre-filtered overdrive tone. Using this control in conjunction with the Filter control allows for serious tone shaping, by re-introducing the raw signal to balance more extreme Filter settings. EXPRESS YOURSELF All three filter options are fully sweep-able via the EXP jack, using a standard TRS expression pedal or expression device, opening the door to inspiring movement within your overdrive tones. In addition, Polaris is fully compatible with Mission Control for interstellar filter sweeps and dirty auto-filter effects. POLARIS FEATURES FIlter control with 3 depths, all fully sweepable via expression pedal Three position BASS toggle switch for low-end control A smooth, symmetrical clipping style overdrive with a detailed texture True-Bypass switching via soft-click footswitch Requires external 9v DC power supply (center-negative) A CADET SERIES PEDAL The Cadet Series brings Spaceman&rsquo;s signature sonic character to a wider audience through repeatable, SMD-based designs. Classic Spaceman designs with the same attention to tone and detail, these pedals offer consistent availability, accessible pricing, and everyday reliability - without sacrificing the individuality that defines Spaceman. Screen printed faceplates and raw metal enclosures set this series apart. Ideal for working musicians and pedalboard-ready setups, the Cadet Series is where our craft meets practicality. TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS Width: 3.9 inches / 99mm Depth: 4.7 inches / 119 mm Height: 2.3 inches / 59 mm Weight: 12.5 ounces Input Resistance: 1Meg Ohm Bypass Current Draw: 16 mA Engaged Current Draw: 17 mA EXP / Control Voltage : 0-5V DC TRS Jack - Over / Reverse voltage protected Input Voltage: 9v-18v DC, negative center via the 2.1mm jack TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS Width: 3.9 inches / 99 mm Depth: 4.7 inches / 119 mm Height: 2.3 inches ",
